<chapter xml:id="ch-background-research" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Additional Resources</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Below, you will find a listing of articles and books to add to the content we present as part of this project!</p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-background-research-resources">
    <title>Resources</title>
    <p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>
        Black, E. (2001). <pubtitle>IBM and the Holocaust: The Strategic Alliance Between Nazi Germany and America's Most Powerful Corporation</pubtitle>. New York: Crown Publishers.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        Green, A. (2020). <pubtitle>Nazi data science: The dark history that led to modern data laws</pubtitle>. Blog. Link: <url href="https://www.magellantv.com/articles/nazi-data-science-the-dark-history-that-led-to-modern-data-laws" visual="www.magellantv.com/articles/nazi-data-science-the-dark-history-that-led-to-modern-data-laws">Nazi Data Science</url>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        Katz, E. (2006). On the neutrality of technology: The Holocaust death camps as a counter-example. <pubtitle>Journal of Genocide Research</pubtitle>, vol. 7, iss. 3, pgs. 409-421. Link: <url href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14623520500190363" visual="www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14623520500190363">tandfonline.com</url>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        Katz, E. (2011). The Nazi engineers: Reflections on technological ethics in hell. <pubtitle>Science and Engineering Ethics</pubtitle>, vol. 17, pgs. 571-582. Link: <url href="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11948-010-9229-z" visual="link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11948-010-9229-z">springer.com</url>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        Lopez-Munoz, F., Alamo, C., Garcia-Garcia, O., Molina, J.D., and Rubio, G. (2008). The role of psychopharmacology in medical abuses of the Third Reich: From euthanasia programmes to human experimentation. <pubtitle>Brain Research Bulletin</pubtitle>, vol. 77, iss. 6, pgs. 388-403. Link: <url href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0361923008003109" visual="www.sciencedirect.com">sciencedirect.com</url>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        From Allianz' website: <url href="https://www.allianz.com/content/dam/onemarketing/azcom/Allianz_com/about-us/who-we-are/documents/Allianz_during_the_Nazi_era.pdf" visual="www.allianz.com/content/dam/.../Allianz_during_the_Nazi_era.pdf">Allianz during the Nazi era (PDF)</url>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</p>
  </section>
</chapter>
